    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1029">

                <pb facs="0953" n="941" sameAs="frus:frus1939v01/pg941"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.6354/167: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-01T17:00:00+01:00">November 1, 1939—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 1—12:53 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2238. I had an opportunity of seeing Malcolm MacDonald last night and having a
                    talk with him about the tin situation and his office telephoned today to say
                    that the Dutch had withdrawn their objection to the British proposal and that
                    therefore the Chairman’s communiqué had been issued raising the tin quota for
                    the current quota [<hi rendition="#italic">quarter</hi>] to 100% and for the
                    first quarter of 1940 to not less than 60%. Please inform Commerce of quota
                    changes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
